00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:19.000
When the Vineland Boys refused to pay their taxes, they were denounced by La AME, and in 1999 the group's founder was murdered by rival gangs. Following his death, several senior members, dubbed shock callers, controlled and regulated the gang's activities. In the early 2000s, the Vineland Boys attempted to smooth things over with La AME. During their efforts to ingratiate themselves back into the fold, they established a reputation for extreme violence and recklessness, with their members considered some of the most dangerous in the city.
当瓦兰德男孩帮拒绝纳税时，他们受到了La AME的谴责，1999年，该集团的创始人被敌对帮派谋杀。在他死后，几位被称为“震撼呼叫者”的高级成员控制并规范了该帮派的活动。在20世纪20年代初，瓦兰德男孩帮曾试图与La AME缓和关系。在他们试图重新博取信任的过程中，他们以极端暴力和鲁莽而闻名，其成员被认为是该市最危险的人员之一。

