00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Unlike other gangs, the Vineland Boys didn't wear uniforms or identify themselves with a specific colour. Instead, they dressed as though they were businessmen. By 2002, the gang comprised mainly of Latin Americans who controlled much of the San Fernando Valley and Burbank drug trade and engaged in murder, narcotics trafficking, money laundering, racketeering and witness intimidation. The gang's leaders enforced harsh discipline among their members and associates, often assaulting or killing those who violated their organization's rules.
与其他帮派不同，瓦兰德男孩帮不穿制服，也不用特定的颜色来标明身份。相反，他们穿得像商人一样。到2002年，该帮派主要由拉丁美洲人组成，他们控制了圣费尔南多谷和伯班克的大部分毒品交易，并从事谋杀、贩毒、洗钱、敲诈勒索和恐吓证人等活动。帮派头目对成员和同伙实行严厉的纪律，经常殴打或杀害违反组织规则的人。

