On Saturday, November 23, 2002, three members of the Vineland Boys were out driving after a birthday celebration at the graveside of a fallen member. Inebriated from consuming a mix of alcohol and drugs, the trio drove along Lancashire Boulevard in North Hollywood and came across 26-year-old Enrique Acosta sitting in his car. They decided to confront him, demanding to know where he was from. Enrique replied, Canoga Park, naming territory that belonged to a rival gang. In response, one of the Vineland Boys pulled out a 9mm handgun and shot him dead.
